   "date": "2014-09-05T17:27:10Z",
   "subject": "Announcing Packrat 0.4.1-1 on CRAN!",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">We’re happy to announce that Packrat is now on CRAN, with version 0.4.1-1!</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">In particular, this release provides better support for local repositories. Local repositories are just folders containing package sources (currently as folders themselves).<br>One can now specify local repositories on a per-project basis by using:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">packrat::set_opts(local.repos = &lt;pathToRepo&gt;)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">and then using <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::install_local(&lt;pkgName&gt;)</code> to install that package from the local repository.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">There is also experimental support for a global ‘cache’ of packages, which can be used across projects. If you wish to enable this feature, you can use (note that it is disabled by default):</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre;overflow:auto;border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">packrat::set_opts(use.cache = TRUE)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">in <strong>each project</strong> where you would utilize the cache. By doing so, if one project installs or uses e.g. Shiny 0.10.1 for CRAN, and another version uses that same package, packrat will look up the installed version of that package in the cache — this should greatly speed up <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat::init()</code>s for new projects that use projects overlapping with other packrat projects with large, overlapping dependency chains.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">In addition, this release provides a number of usability improvements and bug fixes for Windows.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Release notes follow:</p>\r\n<h1 style=\"margin:1.3em 0px 1em;padding:0px;font-weight:bold;font-size:1.6em;border-bottom-width:1px;border-bottom-style:solid;border-bottom-color:rgb(221,221,221)\">Packrat 0.4.1</h1>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Coincides with first CRAN release of packrat.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Disabled migration warnings on Windows (as we now use junction points if<br>possible to facilitate isolation)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Fix bug with <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">tar</code> and projects containing a large number of files (#129)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">External packages (alongside their dependencies) are now symlinked to the<br><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat/lib-ext</code> folder — this allows external packages to function better<br>alongside regular packrat workflows.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">If package symlinking (junctioning) fails, we instead copy the package to<br>the corresponding packrat <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">lib*</code> folder.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h1 style=\"margin:1.3em 0px 1em;padding:0px;font-weight:bold;font-size:1.6em;border-bottom-width:1px;border-bottom-style:solid;border-bottom-color:rgb(221,221,221)\">Packrat 0.4.0</h1>\r\n<ul style=\"margin:1.2em 0px;padding-left:2em\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">The <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">source.packages</code> argument for <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">init</code> and <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">snapshot</code> has now been<br>removed. In lieu, projects can now specify local repositories — packages<br>will be looked up in these directories when attempting to use a source<br>package.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Added <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">install_local</code> for installing packages from local repositories. For<br>example, <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">install_local(&quot;abc&quot;)</code> will attempt to find and install a package<br>named <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">abc</code> from the local repositories as specified within <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">packrat.opts</code>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Added option <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">use.cache</code>, for creating a persistent global cache of<br>installed packages which can be easily symlinked and reused across multiple<br>projects. When active, this will force installation of one version of a<br>package only once — thereafter, any projects requiring that package can<br>symlink to the installed version in the cache.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Use junction points on Windows to enable caching of packages.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Added <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">opts</code> as an object for conveniently getting / setting specific<br>options. For example, calling <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">opts$auto.snapshot()</code> returns the current<br>value for the <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">auto.snapshot</code> option, while <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">opts$auto.snapshot(TRUE)</code> sets<br><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">auto.snapshot</code> on.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Fixed spurious <code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-top-left-radius:3px;border-top-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-right-radius:3px;border-bottom-left-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248)\">download.file</code> warnings on Windows.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:0.5em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important;margin:0.5em 0px!important\">Errors when installing packages on Windows are now captured and reported to<br>the user.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:V2UncmUgaGFwcHkgdG8gYW5ub3VuY2UgdGhhdCBQYWNrcmF0IGlzIG5vdyBvbiBDUkFOLCB3aXRo\r\nIHZlcnNpb24gMC40LjEtMSE8ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PkluIHBhcnRpY3VsYXIsIHRoaXMg\r\ncmVsZWFzZSBwcm92aWRlcyBiZXR0ZXIgc3VwcG9ydCBmb3IgbG9jYWwgcmVwb3NpdG9yaWVzLiBM\r\nb2NhbCByZXBvc2l0b3JpZXMgYXJlIGp1c3QgZm9sZGVycyBjb250YWluaW5nIHBhY2thZ2Ugc291\r\ncmNlcyAoY3VycmVudGx5IGFzIGZvbGRlcnMgdGhlbXNlbHZlcykuPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5PbmUgY2Fu\r\nIG5vdyBzcGVjaWZ5IGxvY2FsIHJlcG9zaXRvcmllcyBvbiBhIHBlci1wcm9qZWN0IGJhc2lzIGJ5\r\nIHVzaW5nOjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyBwYWNrcmF0Ojpz\r\